  "sample_source": "https://sembiance.com/fileFormatSamples/audio/prolineVoice/ (DEX.PVD etc.; samples NOT committed - WAVs regenerable via committed decoder)",
  "rate_decision": {
    "default": 20502,
    "basis": "header byte 0x17 = 0xAD = 173 constant in 5/5 files; Paula PAL clock 3546895/173 = 20501.7 Hz (NTSC 20685.0); Amiga-native formats store the Paula period, and this sits exactly where a fixed hardware parameter would live",
    "alternatives": {
      "20685_ntsc": "same period under NTSC clock; indistinguishable without hardware",
      "8000": "no supporting evidence anywhere in header; makes UI clips 0.10-2.54 s (less plausible); KMERA/GELD content reaches Nyquist with no anti-alias cutoff under 8 kHz - unusual",
      "11025_stereo": "declared by the WAVE header embedded INSIDE BOMB.pvd audio (fmt fully consistent: 11025 Hz, 2ch, 8bit, byterate 22050) - but only 1/5 files carries it, BOMB/DIA show stereo L=R duplication (corr 0.999, exact-equal 0.81/0.82) while KMERA/GELD/JUBEL are native mono (pairing 13-44%, corr 0.23) -> per-file WAV-import artifact, not the format"
    },
    "listening_proxy": "content is broadband BBS UI sound effects (KMERA=Kamera/camera, GELD=money, JUBEL=cheering, BOMB, DIA; German filenames): spectral support extends to ~Nyquist at ANY hypothesized rate (f99.5%=0.29-0.49 cycles/sample), so aliasing/formant analysis cannot settle the rate; 20502 recommended, marked UNRESOLVED-BY-LISTENING"
  },
